From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/realtek: fix RTL8197F parent routing values

The RTL8197F interrupt routing register does not number the first listed
parent as route 1.  Its vendor BSP writes the actual MIPS CPU interrupt
number into each IRR nibble: UART0 input 9 is routed with value 2 and
SWCORE input 15 with value 4.

The generic multi-output driver derives the route as output_index + 1.
Since the RTL8197F device tree parent list starts at CPU IRQ2, this made
each child route one CPU line below the chained parent.  The visible
symptoms are a UART without an interrupt entry and an eth0 IRQ counter
that remains at zero.

Offset the logical output index by one for the RTL8197F-compatible
controller.  Other Realtek SoCs retain the existing zero-based output
numbering.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-realtek-rtl.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-realtek-rtl.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-realtek-rtl.c
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@
  * disconnected. Routing values {1..15} connect to output lines {0..14}.
  */
 static int __init setup_parent_interrupts(struct device_node *node, int *parents,
-	unsigned int num_parents)
+	unsigned int num_parents, unsigned int output_offset)
 {
 	struct realtek_ictl_output *outputs;
 	struct realtek_ictl_output *output;
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@
 			goto domain_err;
 
 		output->fwnode = of_node_to_fwnode(node);
-		output->output_index = p;
+		output->output_index = p + output_offset;
 		output->domain = domain;
 
 		irq_set_chained_handler_and_data(parents[p], realtek_irq_dispatch, output);
@@ -309,6 +309,7 @@
 	int parent_irqs[RTL_ICTL_NUM_OUTPUTS];
 	struct of_phandle_args oirq;
 	unsigned int num_parents;
+	unsigned int output_offset = 0;
 	unsigned int soc_irq;
 	unsigned int p;
 	int cpu;
@@ -332,6 +333,14 @@
 	if (cpumask_empty(&realtek_ictl_cpu_configurable))
 		return -ENXIO;
 
+	/*
+	 * RTL8197F IRR values are the MIPS CPU interrupt numbers themselves.
+	 * Its parent list starts at CPU IRQ2, so parent array index 0 must
+	 * program routing value 2 rather than the generic value 1.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(node, "realtek,rtl8197f-intc"))
+		output_offset = 1;
+
 	num_parents = of_irq_count(node);
 	if (num_parents > RTL_ICTL_NUM_OUTPUTS) {
 		pr_err("too many parent interrupts\n");
@@ -370,7 +379,8 @@
 			return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
-	return setup_parent_interrupts(node, &parent_irqs[0], num_parents);
+	return setup_parent_interrupts(node, &parent_irqs[0], num_parents,
+				       output_offset);
 }
 
 IRQCHIP_DECLARE(realtek_rtl_intc, "realtek,rtl-intc", realtek_rtl_of_init);
